@startuml sd-fault-tolerance-p2
title AISafe - Fault tolerance added in the second delivery (broker, Keycloak DB, empty replica)
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 2
autonumber

actor "Client" as C
participant "Gateway" as G
participant "flight-operations-1" as F1
participant "flight-operations-2" as F2
participant "rabbitmq-1" as R1
participant "rabbitmq-2 / -3" as R23
participant "Keycloak" as K
database "keycloak-db\nprimary" as KP
database "keycloak-db\nstandby" as KS

== 1. One broker node fails ==
R1 -[#red]-> R1 : node down
F1 -> R23 : reconnects to another node of the list (AMQPS)
note over R23 : quorum queues keep working with 2 of 3 nodes
C -> G : POST /api/scheduled-flights
G -> F1 : proxy
F1 --> G : 201 (aggregate + outbox in one transaction)
F1 -> R23 : publish FlightScheduled (publisher confirm)
R23 -> F2 : fo.flights.flight-operations-2
F2 -> F2 : idempotent apply (processed_event, revision)

== 2. The whole broker is down ==
C -> G : POST /api/scheduled-flights
G -> F1 : proxy
F1 --> G : 201: the write does not depend on the broker (AP)
F1 -> F1 : event stays in the outbox; retries with backoff (max 30 s)
C -> G : GET the flight
G -> F2 : proxy
F2 --> G : 404 (eventual consistency: event not delivered yet)
note over R1, R23 : broker restarts
F1 -> R23 : outbox publishes the pending events in order
R23 -> F2 : event delivered
C -> G : GET the flight
G -> F2 : proxy
F2 --> G : 200

== 3. Primary of the Keycloak DB fails ==
KP -[#red]-> KP : down
KS -> KS : repmgr promotes the standby (tested: under 45 s)
C -> G : POST /realms/.../token
G -> K : proxy
K -> KS : new connection (targetServerType=primary)
K --> G : 200 access_token
note over KP : when it returns, the old primary rejoins as a standby

== 4. A FO replica starts with an empty database ==
F2 -> F2 : SnapshotBootstrapper: command store empty
F2 -> F1 : GET /internal/scheduled-flights (X-API-Key)
F1 --> F2 : all flights (FlightState, with revision)
F2 -> F2 : apply each flight (last-writer-wins), in parallel with its queue backlog
@enduml
